age":8,"uses":406},{"base":"H4648","lemma":"מְפִיבֹשֶׁת","tr":"me·phi·vo·shet","gloss":"Mephibosheth","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":18},{"base":"H9035","lemma":"נוּ","tr":"nu","gloss":"us","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":272},{"base":"H3363","lemma":"יָקַע","tr":"ya·qa","gloss":"to dislocate","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":1075},{"base":"H0996","lemma":"בַּ֫יִן","tr":"ba·yin","gloss":"between","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":407},{"base":"H7105","lemma":"קָצִיר","tr":"qa·tsir","gloss":"harvest","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":54},{"base":"H3083","lemma":"יְהוֹנָתָן","tr":"ye·ho·na·tan","gloss":"Jonathan","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":82},{"base":"H4100","lemma":"מָה","tr":"mah","gloss":"what?","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":752}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JOS","chapter":7,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Israel has sinned; they have transgressed My covenant that I commanded them, and they have taken some of what was devoted to destruction. Indeed, they have stolen and lied, and they have put these things with their own possessions.","from":1},{"book":"JOS","chapter":7,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"This is why the Israelites cannot stand against their enemies. They will turn their backs and run from their enemies, because they themselves have been set apart for destruction. I will no longer be with you unless you remove from among you whatever is devoted to destruction.","from":1},{"book":"1SA","chapter":10,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Samuel said to all the people, “Do you see the one the LORD has chosen? There is no one like him among all the people.” And all the people shouted, “Long live the king!”","from":6},{"book":"1SA","chapter":18,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then Jonathan made a covenant with David because he loved him as himself.","from":7},{"book":"1SA","chapter":18,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So when it was time to give Saulʼs daughter Merab to David, she was given in marriage to Adriel of Meholah.","from":8},{"book":"1SA","chapter":20,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"and do not ever cut off your loving devotion from my household—not even when the LORD cuts off every one of Davidʼs enemies from the face of the earth.”","from":7},{"book":"1SA","chapter":23,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So the two of them made a covenant before the LORD. And David remained in Horesh, while Jonathan went home.","from":7},{"book":"2SA","chapter":3,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now Saul had a concubine named Rizpah, the daughter of Aiah. So Ish-bosheth questioned Abner, “Why did you sleep with my fatherʼs concubine?”","from":8}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":4},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"10-14":{"people":[{"id":"aiah-h0345h","name":"Aiah","kind":"person","brief":"Saul's concubine","count":2,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"rizpah-h7532","name":"Rizpah","kind":"person","brief":"Saul's concubine","count":2,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"saul-h7586g","name":"Saul","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel,","count":4,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"jonathan-h3083h","name":"Jonathan","kind":"person","brief":"David's friend","count":3,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"benjamin-h1144g","name":"Benjamin","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"kish-h7027g","name":"Kish","kind":"person","brief":"Saul's father","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"places":[{"id":"beth-shean-h1052","name":"Beth-shean","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"gilboa-h1533g","name":"Gilboa","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"jabesh-h3003g","name":"Jabesh","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"philistia-h6429","name":"Philistia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"zela-h6762","name":"Zela","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"words":[{"base":"H6106","lemma":"עֶ֫צֶם","tr":"e·tsem","gloss":"bone","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":126},{"base":"H7586","lemma":"שָׁאוּל","tr":"sha·ul","gloss":"Saul","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":406},{"base":"H3083","lemma":"יְהוֹנָתָן","tr":"ye·ho·na·tan","gloss":"Jonathan","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":82},{"base":"H7532","lemma":"רִצְפָּה","tr":"rits·pah","gloss":"Rizpah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H0345","lemma":"אַיָּה","tr":"ay·yah","gloss":"Aiah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H1052","lemma":"בֵּית שְׁאָן","tr":"bet she·an","gloss":"Beth-shean","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":18},{"base":"H6430","lemma":"פְּלִשְׁתִּי","tr":"pe·lish·ti","gloss":"Philistine","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":288},{"base":"H6762","lemma":"צֵלַע","tr":"tse·la","gloss":"Zela","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H8064","lemma":"שָׁמַיִם","tr":"sha·ma·yim","gloss":"heaven","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":421},{"base":"H8511","lemma":"תָּלָא","tr":"ta·la","gloss":"to hang","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":21,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"you must not leave the body on the tree overnight, but you must be sure to bury him that day, because anyone who is hung on a tree is under Godʼs curse. You must not defile the land that the LORD your God is giving you as an inheritance.","from":10},{"book":"JOS","chapter":17,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Within Issachar and Asher, Manasseh was assigned Beth-shean, Ibleam, Dor (that is, Naphath), Endor, Taanach, and Megiddo, each with their surrounding settlements.","from":12},{"book":"JOS","chapter":18,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Zelah, Haeleph, Jebus (that is, Jerusalem), Gibeah, and Kiriath-jearim—fourteen cities, along with their villages. This was the inheritance of the clans of the tribe of Benjamin.","from":14},{"book":"1SA","chapter":31,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"They put his armor in the temple of the Ashtoreths and hung his body on the wall of Beth-shan.","from":12},{"book":"1SA","chapter":31,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Then they took their bones and buried them under the tamarisk tree in Jabesh, and they fasted seven days.","from":12},{"book":"2SA","chapter":24,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And there he built an altar to the LORD and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings. Then the LORD answered the prayers on behalf of the land, and the plague upon Israel was halted.","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":40,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Within three days Pharaoh will lift off your head and hang you on a tree. Then the birds will eat the flesh of your body.”","from":10},{"book":"EXO","chapter":32,"verse":27,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"He told them, “This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘Each of you men is to fasten his sword to his side, go back and forth through the camp from gate to gate, and slay his brother, his friend, and his neighbor.’” The Levites did as Moses commanded, and that day about three thousand of the people fell dead. Afterward, Moses said, “Today you have been ordained for service to the LORD, since each man went against his son and his brother; so the LORD has bestowed a blessing on you this day.”","from":14}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":3}]},"15-22":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":5,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"rapha-h7497a","name":"Rapha","kind":"person","brief":"A gigantic man","count":4,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"ishbi-benob-h3430","name":"Ishbi-benob","kind":"person","brief":"A gigantic man","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"abishai-h0052","name":"Abishai","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"zeruiah-h6870g","name":"Zeruiah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of David","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"hushathites-h2843","name":"Hushathites","kind":"person","brief":"Family of warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"saph-h5593","name":"Saph","kind":"person","brief":"A gigantic man","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"sibbecai-h5444","name":"Sibbecai","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"elhanan-h0445g","name":"Elhanan","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"goliath-h1555","name":"Goliath","kind":"person","brief":"A gigantic man","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"jaare-oregim-h3296","name":"Jaare-oregim","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"lahmi-h3902","name":"Lahmi","kind":"person","brief":"A gigantic man","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"huge-man-h4060g","name":"huge man","kind":"person","brief":"A gigantic man","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"jonadab-h3122g","name":"Jonadab","kind":"person","brief":"David's nephew","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"shimeah-h8093","name":"Shimeah","kind":"person","brief":"David's brother","count":1,"firstVerse":21}],"places":[{"id":"philistia-h6429","name":"Philistia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":4,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"gezer-h1507","name":"Gezer","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"gath-h1661","name":"Gath","kind":"place","brief":"In Philistia","count":3,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"bethlehem-h1035g","name":"Bethlehem","kind":"place","brief":"In Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":19}],"words":[{"base":"H7497","lemma":"רָפָה","tr":"ra·pah","gloss":"Rapha","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":25},{"base":"H6430","lemma":"פְּלִשְׁתִּי","tr":"pe·lish·ti","gloss":"Philistine","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":288},{"base":"H4421","lemma":"מִלְחָמָה","tr":"mil·cha·mah","gloss":"battle","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":319},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":1075},{"base":"H5750","lemma":"עוֹד","tr":"od","gloss":"still","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":490},{"base":"H5221","lemma":"נָכָה","tr":"na·khah","gloss":"to smite","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":500},{"base":"H1359","lemma":"גֹּב","tr":"gov","gloss":"Gob","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H3296","lemma":"יַעֲרֵי אֹרְגִים","tr":"ya·a·re o·re·gim","gloss":"Jaare-oregim","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H3430","lemma":"יִשְׁבּוֹ בְּנֹב","tr":"yish·bo b·nov","gloss":"Ishbi-benob","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H1022","lemma":"בֵּית הַלַּחְמִי","tr":"bet hal·lach·mi","gloss":"Bethlehemite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1KI","chapter":11,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"I will give one tribe to his son, so that My servant David will always have a lamp before Me in Jerusalem, the city where I chose to put My Name.","from":17},{"book":"2SA","chapter":18,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"But the people pleaded, “You must not go out! For if we have to flee, they will pay no attention to us. Even if half of us die, they will not care; but you are worth ten thousand of us. It is better for now if you support us from the city.”","from":17},{"book":"1CH","chapter":11,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Sibbecai the Hushathite, Ilai the Ahohite,","from":18},{"book":"1CH","chapter":20,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So these descendants of Rapha in Gath fell at the hands of David and his servants.","from":22},{"book":"GEN","chapter":6,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The Nephilim were on the earth in those days—and afterward as well—when the sons of God had relations with the daughters of men. And they bore them children who became the mighty men of old, men of renown.","from":16},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"In the fourteenth year, Chedorlaomer and the kings allied with him went out and defeated the Rephaites in Ashteroth-karnaim, the Zuzites in Ham, the Emites in Shaveh-kiriathaim,","from":16},{"book":"NUM","chapter":13,"verse":32,"verseEnd":33,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So they gave the Israelites a bad report about the land that they had spied out: “The land we explored devours its inhabitants, and all the people we saw there are great in stature. We even saw the Nephilim there—the descendants of Anak that come from the Nephilim! We seemed like grasshoppers in our own sight, and we must have seemed the same to them!”","from":16},{"book":"DEU","chapter":1,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Where can we go? Our brothers have made our hearts melt, saying: ‘The people are larger and taller than we are; the cities are large, with walls up to the heavens. We even saw the descendants of the Anakim there.’”","from":16}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2}]}}